{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB13878 - MONDO_5231",
  "verbalization": "Pibrentasvir is implicated in the treatment of Hepatitis C Virus (HCV) infection through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Pibrentasvir is used in the management of Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection, which in turn is linked to other antiviral agents such as Beclabuvir, Ledipasvir, and Boceprevir. These agents are all known to target HCV, indicating a shared mechanism of action in the context of antiviral therapy. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to HCV infection through different antiviral drugs highlights the complexity of the treatment landscape and the potential for Pibrentasvir to be part of a broader therapeutic strategy against HCV. The integration of these indications suggests that Pibrentasvir may play a role in the treatment of HCV by supporting the efficacy of other antiviral agents, potentially through mechanisms that are still under investigation.",
